{
  "//": [
    "Item meshes. These are the DrawMeshInstanced belt items, so every triangle",
    "here is multiplied by several hundred on screen -- this is the one file in",
    "the project where a triangle genuinely costs something.",
    "",
    "Consequently: bevel 0 throughout. A chamfer is 44 triangles against a box's",
    "12, and at 30 cm across on a moving belt nobody will ever see the edge. The",
    "art bible's chamfer rule is about things you stand next to.",
    "",
    "Items are single meshes with no children on purpose. Emissive faces are just",
    "parts on palette row 7 -- an instanced draw cannot carry child transforms.",
    "",
    "The five Sparks form a silhouette ladder that reads as a tech tree even in",
    "grayscale: shard cluster -> riveted can -> coil-wrapped -> fluid vial ->",
    "caged core. If you cannot tell them apart at a glance the ladder has failed.",
    "",
    "Ported from modelgen/gen_items.py. Nominal item size is 0.30 m."
  ],

